-- // MARK: INDENT GUIDE
-- indentation style guide
-- for all awful.key() function calls and their associated end statements.
--
-- pattern explanation:
-- 1. awful.key() calls start at 4-space indentation (one level from the containing scope)
-- 2. the opening parenthesis after awful.key creates a new scope at column 14
-- 3. function() definitions and their body content are indented to 8 spaces (two levels)
-- 4. the "end," statement that closes the function scope must be indent to match the
--    function body indentation level (8 spaces), not the awful.key indentation level
-- 5. the description table { description = "...", group = "..." } follows after the "end, "
--    statement, maintaining the 8-space indentation until the closing
--    parenthesis of the the awful.key() call
-- 6. after the awful.key() call completes (closing parenthesis), the next statement
--    returns to the base 4-space indentation level
--
-- example of correct indentation. each function call is separated by a blank line and has a laconic description of the function call below.
--
--     -- laconic description of the function call below
--     awful.key({ modkey }, "key", function()
--         -- function body content at 8 spaces
--         some_function_call()
--         end, { description = "description text", group = "group_name" }),
--
-- this pattern ensures visual consistency and makes the scope boundaries clear,
-- particularly important for complex key binding configurations with nested scopes.




